---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import alice from "../assets/alice.jpg";
---

<Layout>
  <section class="font-default flex flex-col gap-4 justify-center items-center w-[95%] mx-auto p-12">
    <div class="flex flex-row gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="flex w-1/3 flex-col gap-8 items-center">
        <img src={alice.src} class="w-50 rounded-full" />
        <div class="text-xl bg-white/30 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-2xl rounded-3xl p-8">
          <h1 class="text-center underline decoration-1 underline-offset-3">
            our (small) toolkit
          </h1>
          <ul class="list-disc ml-4">
            <li>design & assets: canva</li>
            <li>development: astro, tailwindcss & flowbite, typescript</li>
            <li>content management: sanity cms</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex w-2/3 flex-col gap-4">
        <p class="text-3xl text-center">
          hi, i'm alice and i'm the founder of bespoken.
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl">
          bespoken was born out of a desire to bring creativity and
          one-of-a-kind, aka bespoke, qualities back to an industry that is
          increasingly focused on optimization and automation at-scale.
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl">
          bespoken is intentionally small and community-oriented. our clients
          are businesses we frequent regularly and people who are making a
          difference in their communties.
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl">
          it might sound weird that we pride ourselves on doing small work, when
          technology can reach massive audiences and make widespread change. we
          believe that change starts within ourselves, the way we work, and our
          surroundings. that's why we refuse to use AI in our creative process.
          we want the human-to-human conversations, the iterative design
          process, and the enjoyment of writing code from scratch. we do
          occasionally use AI to debug small pieces of code, as we believe this
          doesn't inhibit our enjoyment and understanding of our work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
